.RS 4
\fBwindow_creation\fP 
.PP
\fBglfwCreateWindow\fP
.RE
.PP
\fBSince\fP
.RS 4
Added in version 3\&.0\&. Replaces \fRglfwCloseWindow\fP\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBGLFWAPI\fP \fBvoid\fP glfwFocusWindow (\fBGLFWwindow\fP * window)"

.PP
Brings the specified window to front and sets input focus\&. This function brings the specified window to front and sets input focus\&. The window should already be visible and not iconified\&.
.PP
By default, both windowed and full screen mode windows are focused when initially created\&. Set the \fBGLFW_FOCUSED\fP to disable this behavior\&.
.PP
Also by default, windowed mode windows are focused when shown with \fBglfwShowWindow\fP\&. Set the \fBGLFW_FOCUS_ON_SHOW\fP to disable this behavior\&.
.PP
\fBDo not use this function\fP to steal focus from other applications unless you are certain that is what the user wants\&. Focus stealing can be extremely disruptive\&.
.PP
For a less disruptive way of getting the user's attention, see \fBattention requests\fP\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIwindow\fP The window to give input focus\&.
.RE
.PP
@errors Possible errors include \fBGLFW_NOT_INITIALIZED\fP and \fBGLFW_PLATFORM_ERROR\fP\&.
.PP
\fBRemarks\fP
.RS 4
@wayland The compositor will likely ignore focus requests unless another window created by the same application already has input focus\&.
.RE
.PP
@thread_safety This function must only be called from the main thread\&.
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBwindow_focus\fP 
.PP
\fBwindow_attention\fP
.RE
.PP
\fBSince\fP
.RS 4
Added in version 3\&.2\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBGLFWAPI\fP \fBvoid\fP glfwGetFramebufferSize (\fBGLFWwindow\fP * window, int * width, int * height)"

.PP
Retrieves the size of the framebuffer of the specified window\&. This function retrieves the size, in pixels, of the framebuffer of the specified window\&. If you wish to retrieve the size of the window in screen coordinates, see \fBglfwGetWindowSize\fP\&.
.PP
Any or all of the size arguments may be \fRNULL\fP\&. If an error occurs, all non-\fRNULL\fP size arguments will be set to zero\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIwindow\fP The window whose framebuffer to query\&. 
.br
\fIwidth\fP Where to store the width, in pixels, of the framebuffer, or \fRNULL\fP\&. 
.br
\fIheight\fP Where to store the height, in pixels, of the framebuffer, or \fRNULL\fP\&.
.RE
.PP
@errors Possible errors include \fBGLFW_NOT_INITIALIZED\fP and \fBGLFW_PLATFORM_ERROR\fP\&.
.PP
@thread_safety This function must only be called from the main thread\&.
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBwindow_fbsize\fP 
.PP
\fBglfwSetFramebufferSizeCallback\fP
.RE
.PP
\fBSince\fP
.RS 4
Added in version 3\&.0\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBGLFWAPI\fP int glfwGetWindowAttrib (\fBGLFWwindow\fP * window, int attrib)"

.PP
Returns an attribute of the specified window\&. This function returns the value of an attribute of the specified window or its OpenGL or OpenGL ES context\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIwindow\fP The window to query\&. 
.br
\fIattrib\fP The \fBwindow attribute\fP whose value to return\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The value of the attribute, or zero if an \fBerror\fP occurred\&.
.RE
.PP
@errors Possible errors include \fBGLFW_NOT_INITIALIZED\fP, \fBGLFW_INVALID_ENUM\fP and \fBGLFW_PLATFORM_ERROR\fP\&.
.PP
\fBRemarks\fP
.RS 4
Framebuffer related hints are not window attributes\&. See \fBwindow_attribs_fb\fP for more information\&.
.PP
Zero is a valid value for many window and context related attributes so you cannot use a return value of zero as an indication of errors\&. However, this function should not fail as long as it is passed valid arguments and the library has been \fBinitialized\fP\&.
.PP
@wayland The Wayland protocol provides no way to check whether a window is iconfied, so \fBGLFW_ICONIFIED\fP always returns \fRGLFW_FALSE\fP\&.
.RE
.PP
@thread_safety This function must only be called from the main thread\&.
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBwindow_attribs\fP 
.PP
\fBglfwSetWindowAttrib\fP
.RE
.PP
\fBSince\fP
.RS 4
Added in version 3\&.0\&. Replaces \fRglfwGetWindowParam\fP and \fRglfwGetGLVersion\fP\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBGLFWAPI\fP \fBvoid\fP glfwGetWindowContentScale (\fBGLFWwindow\fP * window, float * xscale, float * yscale)"

.PP
Retrieves the content scale for the specified window\&. This function retrieves the content scale for the specified window\&. The content scale is the ratio between the current DPI and the platform's default DPI\&. This is especially important for text and any UI elements\&. If the pixel dimensions of your UI scaled by this look appropriate on your machine then it should appear at a reasonable size on other machines regardless of their DPI and scaling settings\&. This relies on the system DPI and scaling settings being somewhat correct\&.
.PP
On platforms where each monitors can have its own content scale, the window content scale will depend on which monitor the system considers the window to be on\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIwindow\fP The window to query\&. 
.br
\fIxscale\fP Where to store the x-axis content scale, or \fRNULL\fP\&. 
.br
\fIyscale\fP Where to store the y-axis content scale, or \fRNULL\fP\&.
.RE
.PP
@errors Possible errors include \fBGLFW_NOT_INITIALIZED\fP and \fBGLFW_PLATFORM_ERROR\fP\&.
.PP
@thread_safety This function must only be called from the main thread\&.
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBwindow_scale\fP 
.PP
\fBglfwSetWindowContentScaleCallback\fP 
.PP
\fBglfwGetMonitorContentScale\fP
.RE
.PP
\fBSince\fP
.RS 4
Added in version 3\&.3\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBGLFWAPI\fP \fBvoid\fP glfwGetWindowFrameSize (\fBGLFWwindow\fP * window, int * left, int * top, int * right, int * bottom)"

.PP
Retrieves the size of the frame of the window\&. This function retrieves the size, in screen coordinates, of each edge of the frame of the specified window\&. This size includes the title bar, if the window has one\&. The size of the frame may vary depending on the \fBwindow-related hints\fP used to create it\&.
.PP
Because this function retrieves the size of each window frame edge and not the offset along a particular coordinate axis, the retrieved values will always be zero or positive\&.
.PP
Any or all of the size arguments may be \fRNULL\fP\&. If an error occurs, all non-\fRNULL\fP size arguments will be set to zero\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIwindow\fP The window whose frame size to query\&. 
.br
\fIleft\fP Where to store the size, in screen coordinates, of the left edge of the window frame, or \fRNULL\fP\&. 
.br
\fItop\fP Where to store the size, in screen coordinates, of the top edge of the window frame, or \fRNULL\fP\&. 
.br
\fIright\fP Where to store the size, in screen coordinates, of the right edge of the window frame, or \fRNULL\fP\&. 
.br
\fIbottom\fP Where to store the size, in screen coordinates, of the bottom edge of the window frame, or \fRNULL\fP\&.
.RE
.PP
@errors Possible errors include \fBGLFW_NOT_INITIALIZED\fP and \fBGLFW_PLATFORM_ERROR\fP\&.
.PP
@thread_safety This function must only be called from the main thread\&.
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBwindow_size\fP
.RE
.PP
\fBSince\fP
.RS 4
Added in version 3\&.1\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBGLFWAPI\fP \fBGLFWmonitor\fP * glfwGetWindowMonitor (\fBGLFWwindow\fP * window)"

.PP
Returns the monitor that the window uses for full screen mode\&. This function returns the handle of the monitor that the specified window is in full screen on\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIwindow\fP The window to query\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The monitor, or \fRNULL\fP if the window is in windowed mode or an \fBerror\fP occurred\&.
.RE
.PP
@errors Possible errors include \fBGLFW_NOT_INITIALIZED\fP\&.
.PP
@thread_safety This function must only be called from the main thread\&.
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBwindow_monitor\fP 
.PP
\fBglfwSetWindowMonitor\fP
.RE
.PP
\fBSince\fP
.RS 4
Added in version 3\&.0\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBGLFWAPI\fP float glfwGetWindowOpacity (\fBGLFWwindow\fP * window)"

.PP
Returns the opacity of the whole window\&. This function returns the opacity of the window, including any decorations\&.
.PP
The opacity (or alpha) value is a positive finite number between zero and one, where zero is fully transparent and one is fully opaque\&. If the system does not support whole window transparency, this function always returns one\&.
.PP
The initial opacity value for newly created windows is one\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIwindow\fP The window to query\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The opacity value of the specified window\&.
.RE
.PP
@errors Possible errors include \fBGLFW_NOT_INITIALIZED\fP and \fBGLFW_PLATFORM_ERROR\fP\&.
.PP
@thread_safety This function must only be called from the main thread\&.
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBwindow_transparency\fP 
.PP
\fBglfwSetWindowOpacity\fP
.RE
.PP
\fBSince\fP
.RS 4
Added in version 3\&.3\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBGLFWAPI\fP \fBvoid\fP glfwGetWindowPos (\fBGLFWwindow\fP * window, int * xpos, int * ypos)"

.PP
Retrieves the position of the content area of the specified window\&. This function retrieves the position, in screen coordinates, of the upper-left corner of the content area of the specified window\&.
.PP
Any or all of the position arguments may be \fRNULL\fP\&. If an error occurs, all non-\fRNULL\fP position arguments will be set to zero\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIwindow\fP The window to query\&. 
.br
\fIxpos\fP Where to store the x-coordinate of the upper-left corner of the content area, or \fRNULL\fP\&. 
.br
\fIypos\fP Where to store the y-coordinate of the upper-left corner of the content area, or \fRNULL\fP\&.
.RE
.PP
@errors Possible errors include \fBGLFW_NOT_INITIALIZED\fP, \fBGLFW_PLATFORM_ERROR\fP and \fBGLFW_FEATURE_UNAVAILABLE\fP (see remarks)\&.
.PP
\fBRemarks\fP
.RS 4
@wayland There is no way for an application to retrieve the global position of its windows\&. This function will emit \fBGLFW_FEATURE_UNAVAILABLE\fP\&.
.RE
.PP
@thread_safety This function must only be called from the main thread\&.
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBwindow_pos\fP 
.PP
\fBglfwSetWindowPos\fP
.RE
.PP
\fBSince\fP
.RS 4
Added in version 3\&.0\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBGLFWAPI\fP \fBvoid\fP glfwGetWindowSize (\fBGLFWwindow\fP * window, int * width, int * height)"

.PP
Retrieves the size of the content area of the specified window\&. This function retrieves the size, in screen coordinates, of the content area of the specified window\&. If you wish to retrieve the size of the framebuffer of the window in pixels, see \fBglfwGetFramebufferSize\fP\&.
.PP
Any or all of the size arguments may be \fRNULL\fP\&. If an error occurs, all non-\fRNULL\fP size arguments will be set to zero\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIwindow\fP The window whose size to retrieve\&. 
.br
\fIwidth\fP Where to store the width, in screen coordinates, of the content area, or \fRNULL\fP\&. 
.br
\fIheight\fP Where to store the height, in screen coordinates, of the content area, or \fRNULL\fP\&.
.RE
.PP
@errors Possible errors include \fBGLFW_NOT_INITIALIZED\fP and \fBGLFW_PLATFORM_ERROR\fP\&.
.PP
@thread_safety This function must only be called from the main thread\&.
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBwindow_size\fP 
.PP
\fBglfwSetWindowSize\fP
.RE
.PP
\fBSince\fP
.RS 4
Added in version 1\&.0\&. @glfw3 Added window handle parameter\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBGLFWAPI\fP const char * glfwGetWindowTitle (\fBGLFWwindow\fP * window)"

.PP
Returns the title of the specified window\&. This function returns the window title, encoded as UTF-8, of the specified window\&. This is the title set previously by \fBglfwCreateWindow\fP or \fBglfwSetWindowTitle\fP\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIwindow\fP The window to query\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The UTF-8 encoded window title, or \fRNULL\fP if an \fBerror\fP occurred\&.
.RE
.PP
@errors Possible errors include \fBGLFW_NOT_INITIALIZED\fP\&.
.PP
\fBRemarks\fP
.RS 4
The returned title is currently a copy of the title last set by \fBglfwCreateWindow\fP or \fBglfwSetWindowTitle\fP\&. It does not include any additional text which may be appended by the platform or another program\&.
.RE
.PP
@pointer_lifetime The returned string is allocated and freed by GLFW\&. You should not free it yourself\&. It is valid until the next call to \fBglfwGetWindowTitle\fP or \fBglfwSetWindowTitle\fP, or until the library is terminated\&.
.PP
@thread_safety This function must only be called from the main thread\&.
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBwindow_title\fP 
.PP
\fBglfwSetWindowTitle\fP
.RE
.PP
\fBSince\fP
.RS 4
Added in version 3\&.4\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBGLFWAPI\fP \fBvoid\fP * glfwGetWindowUserPointer (\fBGLFWwindow\fP * window)"

.PP
Returns the user pointer of the specified window\&. This function returns the current value of the user-defined pointer of the specified window\&. The initial value is \fRNULL\fP\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIwindow\fP The window whose pointer to return\&.
.RE
.PP
@errors Possible errors include \fBGLFW_NOT_INITIALIZED\fP\&.
.PP
@thread_safety This function may be called from any thread\&. Access is not synchronized\&.
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBwindow_userptr\fP 
.PP
\fBglfwSetWindowUserPointer\fP
.RE
.PP
\fBSince\fP
.RS 4
Added in version 3\&.0\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBGLFWAPI\fP \fBvoid\fP glfwHideWindow (\fBGLFWwindow\fP * window)"

.PP
Hides the specified window\&. This function hides the specified window if it was previously visible\&. If the window is already hidden or is in full screen mode, this function does nothing\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIwindow\fP The window to hide\&.
.RE
.PP
@errors Possible errors include \fBGLFW_NOT_INITIALIZED\fP and \fBGLFW_PLATFORM_ERROR\fP\&.
.PP
@thread_safety This function must only be called from the main thread\&.
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBwindow_hide\fP 
.PP
\fBglfwShowWindow\fP
.RE
.PP
\fBSince\fP
.RS 4
Added in version 3\&.0\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBGLFWAPI\fP \fBvoid\fP glfwIconifyWindow (\fBGLFWwindow\fP * window)"

.PP
Iconifies the specified window\&. This function iconifies (minimizes) the specified window if it was previously restored\&. If the window is already iconified, this function does nothing\&.
.PP
If the specified window is a full screen window, GLFW restores the original video mode of the monitor\&. The window's desired video mode is set again when the window is restored\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIwindow\fP The window to iconify\&.
.RE
.PP
@errors Possible errors include \fBGLFW_NOT_INITIALIZED\fP and \fBGLFW_PLATFORM_ERROR\fP\&.
.PP
\fBRemarks\fP
.RS 4
@wayland Once a window is iconified, \fBglfwRestoreWindow\fP won’t be able to restore it\&. This is a design decision of the xdg-shell protocol\&.
.RE
.PP
@thread_safety This function must only be called from the main thread\&.
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBwindow_iconify\fP 
.PP
\fBglfwRestoreWindow\fP 
.PP
\fBglfwMaximizeWindow\fP
.RE
.PP
\fBSince\fP
.RS 4
Added in version 2\&.1\&. @glfw3 Added window handle parameter\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBGLFWAPI\fP \fBvoid\fP glfwMaximizeWindow (\fBGLFWwindow\fP * window)"

.PP
Maximizes the specified window\&. This function maximizes the specified window if it was previously not maximized\&. If the window is already maximized, this function does nothing\&.
.PP
If the specified window is a full screen window, this function does nothing\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIwindow\fP The window to maximize\&.
.RE
.PP
@errors Possible errors include \fBGLFW_NOT_INITIALIZED\fP and \fBGLFW_PLATFORM_ERROR\fP\&.
.PP
\fBThread Safety\fP
.RS 4
This function may only be called from the main thread\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBwindow_iconify\fP 
.PP
\fBglfwIconifyWindow\fP 
.PP
\fBglfwRestoreWindow\fP
.RE
.PP
\fBSince\fP
.RS 4
Added in GLFW 3\&.2\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBGLFWAPI\fP \fBvoid\fP glfwPollEvents (\fBvoid\fP )"

.PP
Processes all pending events\&. This function processes only those events that are already in the event queue and then returns immediately\&. Processing events will cause the window and input callbacks associated with those events to be called\&.
.PP
On some platforms, a window move, resize or menu operation will cause event processing to block\&. This is due to how event processing is designed on those platforms\&. You can use the \fBwindow refresh callback\fP to redraw the contents of your window when necessary during such operations\&.
.PP
Do not assume that callbacks you set will \fIonly\fP be called in response to event processing functions like this one\&. While it is necessary to poll for events, window systems that require GLFW to register callbacks of its own can pass events to GLFW in response to many window system function calls\&. GLFW will pass those events on to the application callbacks before returning\&.
.PP
\fBEvent\fP processing is not required for joystick input to work\&.
.PP
@errors Possible errors include \fBGLFW_NOT_INITIALIZED\fP and \fBGLFW_PLATFORM_ERROR\fP\&.
.PP
@reentrancy This function must not be called from a callback\&.
.PP
@thread_safety This function must only be called from the main thread\&.
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBevents\fP 
.PP
\fBglfwWaitEvents\fP 
.PP
\fBglfwWaitEventsTimeout\fP
.RE
.PP
\fBSince\fP
.RS 4
Added in version 1\&.0\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBGLFWAPI\fP \fBvoid\fP glfwPostEmptyEvent (\fBvoid\fP )"

.PP
Posts an empty event to the event queue\&. This function posts an empty event from the current thread to the event queue, causing \fBglfwWaitEvents\fP or \fBglfwWaitEventsTimeout\fP to return\&.
.PP
@errors Possible errors include \fBGLFW_NOT_INITIALIZED\fP and \fBGLFW_PLATFORM_ERROR\fP\&.
.PP
@thread_safety This function may be called from any thread\&.
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBevents\fP 
.PP
\fBglfwWaitEvents\fP 
.PP
\fBglfwWaitEventsTimeout\fP
.RE
.PP
\fBSince\fP
.RS 4
Added in version 3\&.1\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBGLFWAPI\fP \fBvoid\fP glfwRequestWindowAttention (\fBGLFWwindow\fP * window)"

.PP
Requests user attention to the specified window\&. This function requests user attention to the specified window\&. On platforms where this is not supported, attention is requested to the application as a whole\&.
.PP
Once the user has given attention, usually by focusing the window or application, the system will end the request automatically\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIwindow\fP The window to request attention to\&.
.RE
.PP
@errors Possible errors include \fBGLFW_NOT_INITIALIZED\fP and \fBGLFW_PLATFORM_ERROR\fP\&.
.PP
\fBRemarks\fP
.RS 4
@macos Attention is requested to the application as a whole, not the specific window\&.
.RE
.PP
@thread_safety This function must only be called from the main thread\&.
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBwindow_attention\fP
.RE
.PP
\fBSince\fP
.RS 4
Added in version 3\&.3\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBGLFWAPI\fP \fBvoid\fP glfwRestoreWindow (\fBGLFWwindow\fP * window)"

.PP
Restores the specified window\&. This function restores the specified window if it was previously iconified (minimized) or maximized\&. If the window is already restored, this function does nothing\&.
.PP
If the specified window is an iconified full screen window, its desired video mode is set again for its monitor when the window is restored\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIwindow\fP The window to restore\&.
.RE
.PP
@errors Possible errors include \fBGLFW_NOT_INITIALIZED\fP and \fBGLFW_PLATFORM_ERROR\fP\&.
.PP
@thread_safety This function must only be called from the main thread\&.
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBwindow_iconify\fP 
.PP
\fBglfwIconifyWindow\fP 
.PP
\fBglfwMaximizeWindow\fP
.RE
.PP
\fBSince\fP
.RS 4
Added in version 2\&.1\&. @glfw3 Added window handle parameter\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBGLFWAPI\fP \fBGLFWframebuffersizefun\fP glfwSetFramebufferSizeCallback (\fBGLFWwindow\fP * window, \fBGLFWframebuffersizefun\fP callback)"

.PP
Sets the framebuffer resize callback for the specified window\&. This function sets the framebuffer resize callback of the specified window, which is called when the framebuffer of the specified window is resized\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIwindow\fP The window whose callback to set\&. 
.br
\fIcallback\fP The new callback, or \fRNULL\fP to remove the currently set callback\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The previously set callback, or \fRNULL\fP if no callback was set or the library had not been \fBinitialized\fP\&.
.RE
.PP
@callback_signature 
.PP
.nf
void function_name(GLFWwindow* window, int width, int height)

.fi
.PP
 For more information about the callback parameters, see the \fBfunction pointer type\fP\&.
.PP
@errors Possible errors include \fBGLFW_NOT_INITIALIZED\fP\&.
.PP
@thread_safety This function must only be called from the main thread\&.
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBwindow_fbsize\fP
.RE
.PP
\fBSince\fP
.RS 4
Added in version 3\&.0\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBGLFWAPI\fP \fBvoid\fP glfwSetWindowAspectRatio (\fBGLFWwindow\fP * window, int numer, int denom)"

.PP
Sets the aspect ratio of the specified window\&. This function sets the required aspect ratio of the content area of the specified window\&. If the window is full screen, the aspect ratio only takes effect once it is made windowed\&. If the window is not resizable, this function does nothing\&.
.PP
The aspect ratio is specified as a numerator and a denominator and both values must be greater than zero\&. For example, the common 16:9 aspect ratio is specified as 16 and 9, respectively\&.
.PP
If the numerator and denominator is set to \fRGLFW_DONT_CARE\fP then the aspect ratio limit is disabled\&.
.PP
The aspect ratio is applied immediately to a windowed mode window and may cause it to be resized\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIwindow\fP The window to set limits for\&. 
.br
\fInumer\fP The numerator of the desired aspect ratio, or \fRGLFW_DONT_CARE\fP\&. 
.br
\fIdenom\fP The denominator of the desired aspect ratio, or \fRGLFW_DONT_CARE\fP\&.
.RE
.PP
@errors Possible errors include \fBGLFW_NOT_INITIALIZED\fP, \fBGLFW_INVALID_VALUE\fP and \fBGLFW_PLATFORM_ERROR\fP\&.
.PP
\fBRemarks\fP
.RS 4
If you set size limits and an aspect ratio that conflict, the results are undefined\&.
.PP
@wayland The aspect ratio will not be applied until the window is actually resized, either by the user or by the compositor\&.
.RE
.PP
@thread_safety This function must only be called from the main thread\&.
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBwindow_sizelimits\fP 
.PP
\fBglfwSetWindowSizeLimits\fP
.RE
.PP
\fBSince\fP
.RS 4
Added in version 3\&.2\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBGLFWAPI\fP \fBvoid\fP glfwSetWindowAttrib (\fBGLFWwindow\fP * window, int attrib, int value)"

.PP
Sets an attribute of the specified window\&. This function sets the value of an attribute of the specified window\&.
.PP
The supported attributes are \fBGLFW_DECORATED\fP, \fBGLFW_RESIZABLE\fP, \fBGLFW_FLOATING\fP, \fBGLFW_AUTO_ICONIFY\fP and \fBGLFW_FOCUS_ON_SHOW\fP\&. \fBGLFW_MOUSE_PASSTHROUGH\fP
.PP
Some of these attributes are ignored for full screen windows\&. The new value will take effect if the window is later made windowed\&.
.PP
Some of these attributes are ignored for windowed mode windows\&. The new value will take effect if the window is later made full screen\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIwindow\fP The window to set the attribute for\&. 
.br
\fIattrib\fP A supported window attribute\&. 
.br
\fIvalue\fP \fRGLFW_TRUE\fP or \fRGLFW_FALSE\fP\&.
.RE
.PP
@errors Possible errors include \fBGLFW_NOT_INITIALIZED\fP, \fBGLFW_INVALID_ENUM\fP, \fBGLFW_INVALID_VALUE\fP, \fBGLFW_PLATFORM_ERROR\fP and \fBGLFW_FEATURE_UNAVAILABLE\fP (see remarks)\&.
.PP
\fBRemarks\fP
.RS 4
Calling \fBglfwGetWindowAttrib\fP will always return the latest value, even if that value is ignored by the current mode of the window\&.
.PP
@wayland The \fBGLFW_FLOATING\fP window attribute is not supported\&. Setting this will emit \fBGLFW_FEATURE_UNAVAILABLE\fP\&.
.RE
.PP
@thread_safety This function must only be called from the main thread\&.
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBwindow_attribs\fP 
