.SS "\fBGLFWAPI\fP \fBvoid\fP glfwSetWindowIcon (\fBGLFWwindow\fP * window, int count, const \fBGLFWimage\fP * images)"

.PP
Sets the icon for the specified window\&. This function sets the icon of the specified window\&. If passed an array of candidate images, those of or closest to the sizes desired by the system are selected\&. If no images are specified, the window reverts to its default icon\&.
.PP
The pixels are 32-bit, little-endian, non-premultiplied RGBA, i\&.e\&. eight bits per channel with the red channel first\&. They are arranged canonically as packed sequential rows, starting from the top-left corner\&.
.PP
The desired image sizes varies depending on platform and system settings\&. The selected images will be rescaled as needed\&. Good sizes include 16x16, 32x32 and 48x48\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIwindow\fP The window whose icon to set\&. 
.br
\fIcount\fP The number of images in the specified array, or zero to revert to the default window icon\&. 
.br
\fIimages\fP The images to create the icon from\&. This is ignored if count is zero\&.
.RE
.PP
@errors Possible errors include \fBGLFW_NOT_INITIALIZED\fP, \fBGLFW_INVALID_VALUE\fP, \fBGLFW_PLATFORM_ERROR\fP and \fBGLFW_FEATURE_UNAVAILABLE\fP (see remarks)\&.
.PP
@pointer_lifetime The specified image data is copied before this function returns\&.
.PP
\fBRemarks\fP
.RS 4
@macos Regular windows do not have icons on macOS\&. This function will emit \fBGLFW_FEATURE_UNAVAILABLE\fP\&. The dock icon will be the same as the application bundle's icon\&. For more information on bundles, see the \fRBundle Programming Guide\fP in the Mac Developer Library\&.
.PP
@wayland There is no existing protocol to change an icon, the window will thus inherit the one defined in the application's desktop file\&. This function will emit \fBGLFW_FEATURE_UNAVAILABLE\fP\&.
.RE
.PP
@thread_safety This function must only be called from the main thread\&.
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBwindow_icon\fP
.RE
.PP
\fBSince\fP
.RS 4
Added in version 3\&.2\&. 
.RE
.PP

